// KycState is where a user's identity verification with Coinbase stands for
// one product, and what they still have to provide for it. It carries nothing
// the user submitted and no reason for any decision: Coinbase gives none, and
// clients must not guess at one or show one.
//
// Coinbase has no single verdict on a user. It grants or refuses each of the
// things a user may do with it, and each product needs a set of them. The
// status is the product's set seen as one. A user is NOT_STARTED for a
// product until StartKyc has Coinbase asked for all of its set. After that
// they are VERIFIED when all of the set is granted and BLOCKED when any of it
// is refused, and otherwise ACTION_REQUIRED while requirements lists
// something and IN_REVIEW while it lists nothing.
